@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml
title System Dependence Graph overlay construction

skinparam backgroundColor #FCFCFC
skinparam component {
  BorderColor #343A40
  FontColor #212529
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #F8F9FA
  BorderColor #495057
}

component "Resolved call topology\nCallSite · StaticCall · DynamicCall" as CALLS #DBE4FF
component "Interprocedural DFG\nactual → formal: Parameter\nreturn expression → call: ReturnValue" as DFG #D3F9D8
component "Per-function PDG\nControlDependence\nDataDependence" as PDG #FFF3BF
component "EffectSummary map\n<latex>M_f = \mathtt{param\_to\_return}</latex>" as EFFECT #E5DBFF
component "build_summary_edges\nresolved target union\nsorted labeled uniqueness" as BUILD #FFE8CC
component "Unified CodePropertyGraph\none shared node set" as CPG #C3FAE8
component "SDG summary overlay\nactual → call\nDataDependence(label=summary)" as SUMMARY #FCC2D7
component "Two-pass slicer\nBTreeSet<NodeId>\nnode + call-depth caps" as SLICE #FFE3E3

CALLS --> DFG : resolution precedes extraction
CALLS --> BUILD : call → callee
EFFECT --> BUILD : bit <latex>i</latex> selects actual <latex>a_i</latex>
PDG --> CPG : append typed edges
DFG --> CPG : append typed edges
CPG --> BUILD : call arguments / endpoints
BUILD --> SUMMARY : append only
SUMMARY --> CPG : same nodes, labeled edge
CPG --> SLICE : PDG + Parameter + ReturnValue + summary

note bottom of BUILD
  A capped effect summary connects every actual.
  A truncated mask connects positions beyond bit 63.
  Repeating the builder adds zero edges.
end note

note bottom of SLICE
  The slicer reads graph evidence only.
  It does not parse source and does not create a parallel graph.
end note

legend bottom
|= Colour |= Meaning |
|<#DBE4FF>| resolved call evidence |
|<#D3F9D8>| parameter and return value flow |
|<#FFF3BF>| intraprocedural dependence |
|<#E5DBFF>| procedure effect summaries |
|<#FFE8CC>| deterministic construction |
|<#C3FAE8>| unified CPG storage |
|<#FCC2D7>| caller-local summary dependence |
|<#FFE3E3>| bounded public slice |
endlegend
@enduml
